  "id": "retrograde-transport",
  "term": "retrograde transport",
  "definition": "Retrograde transport is a cellular recycling process in which material taken in from the cell surface is moved from early endosomes to the Golgi and then returned to the plasma membrane. It helps recycle certain membrane cargo, such as receptor proteins.",
